Ethernet is the most common type.
Ethernet has standards that's maintained by IEEE committee
IEEE Standards (Sample)
  -1000BASE-T|Gigabit Ethernet|Copper Wire|1 gigabit per sec
  -10GBASE-T|10 Gigabit Ethernet|Copper Wire|10 gigabits per sec
  -1000BASE-SX|Gigabit Ethernet|Fiber Optics|1 gigabit per sec
Deciphering the standard
  -Speed, Signal, Media
  -BASE is baseband
  -T is twisted pair copper|F is fiber|SX short wavelength light

Fiber Communication
  -very secure and difficult to tap into
  -used in long distances due to slow degradation
  -immune to radio interference
  -Ferrule is where the outside coating lays
  -Fiber Core is where the light bounces
Types of fiber optic cables
  -multimode fiber is used for short-range communication
    -inexpensive light source like LED
    -several lights can be passed
  -Single-mode fiber
    -up to 100km without regenerating the signal
    -uses expensive light source like lazer
    -only one light beam
Cabeling is the backbone of networking
  -twisted pair copper cabling
      -most common
      -TRANSMIT+, TRANSMIT-/RECEIVE+,RECEIVE-
      -the twist constantly keeps the signal moving away from interference
      -some pairs have different twist rates
      -Cables don't have any speed
      -the signals have the speed
      -IEEE 802.3 have ethernet standards to determine cable type
